From: GreenAutarky OS <noreply@greenautarky.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] rockchip: rk3328: DSGW-210 stop driving GPIO0_D6
 (vcc_sd/vmmc-supply)

On the Rock64, GPIO0_D6 switches the SD-card supply (vcc_sd, regulator-fixed,
active low) and &sdmmc references it as vmmc-supply. On the DSGW-210 the same
pin is the bq25895 charger INT line, an input. Because u-boot reuses the
rock64 base DTS, the mmc driver enables vcc_sd and u-boot leaves GPIO0_D6
configured as an output when it hands over to Linux.

Drop vmmc-supply from &sdmmc and disable &vcc_sd (also removing the
bootph-pre-ram that put it into the SPL DTB), so neither SPL nor u-boot proper
binds the regulator or touches the pin.

Signed-off-by: GreenAutarky OS <noreply@greenautarky.invalid>
---
diff --git a/arch/arm/dts/rk3328-rock64-u-boot.dtsi b/arch/arm/dts/rk3328-rock64-u-boot.dtsi
index bea476a..5ebfb84 100644
--- a/arch/arm/dts/rk3328-rock64-u-boot.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm/dts/rk3328-rock64-u-boot.dtsi
@@ -99,3 +99,22 @@
 &gmac2io {
 	status = "disabled";
 };
+
+/*
+ * DSGW-210: GPIO0_D6 is the bq25895 charger INT (an input), not the SD-card
+ * power switch it is on the Rock64. The upstream rk3328-rock64.dts declares
+ * vcc_sd as a regulator-fixed on <&gpio0 RK_PD6 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW> and links it
+ * as &sdmmc vmmc-supply, so u-boot (SPL and proper) would probe the
+ * regulator and drive the pin as an OUTPUT. Keep u-boot from touching it:
+ * drop the vmmc-supply link (the only consumer of vcc_sd) and disable the
+ * fixed regulator itself, including the SPL copy that the bootph-pre-ram
+ * above requested.
+ */
+&sdmmc {
+	/delete-property/ vmmc-supply;
+};
+
+&vcc_sd {
+	status = "disabled";
+	/delete-property/ bootph-pre-ram;
+};
